I'm not familiar with th emodel you're trying to estimate
and those are a lot of variables to take in.

Have you tried estimating something simpler and working
up to something of this complexity?

Was your intention to just do the forward sampling for y?
There aren't any other parameters in the model.

Whatever the case, your model block won't work because you
declare a local variable and then use it before defining it:

 int nJ[T];
  eps ~ normal(0,1);
  nJ  ~ poisson(hy);

The sampling statement does not define a variable.  It assumes
the variable is already defined and uses it to increment the overall
log density for the posterior.

- Bob

